Z||000000||rodmcneill||12-25-2001||01:24 AM||||Are there places still offering "lifetime alignments"? You buy the first one at a higher price and then get any others free.||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||12-25-2001||06:59 AM||||I think I remember those. Havent seen any advertised lately, Id guess they lost there butts on that idea. All it would take is a pothole to knock it out. Some states theyd have to give a free alignment once a month, lol  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDude||12-25-2001||07:01 AM||||I'm not sure, but in those places, the tech makes next to nothing for doing those lifetime alignments...so most of them do "next to nothing" too.  I'd stay away from them.<P>Phil Pettus<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||12-25-2001||07:03 AM||||the firestone by me does lifetime for about 110-120 bucks.<P>i havn't brought my car in yet for the 2nd alignment.  So i cant judge how well they keep that policy.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Joe Torma||12-25-2001||10:48 AM||||I bet you'll need ball joints or tie rods every time you go back!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Spiff||12-25-2001||02:26 PM||||I used to have a lifetime alignment for my Eagle Talon. But alas the company (Montgomery Wards) that did the alignment went out of business. So I guess I did have a lifetime Alignment. Not the cars, but the companys.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spiffsig2_18.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||wcapman||12-25-2001||03:45 PM||||I have a lifetime alignment from Firestone.  I know the guys there and they do a quality job.  Since I am constantly changing my alignment specs they see me often.  I'm in the process right now of redesigning the rear suspension...again///so they will probably see me many more times.  They never complain,  but they do work by appt only.  I think if you get to know the guys at the shop they tend to come through for you.  Pick a shop where the guys build their own race cars or something similar. ||||reg||10
Z||000007||fierodoug5||12-25-2001||07:16 PM||||All Firestone stores offer lifetime Alignment. Ask for a Before and After Print-out everytime you get it done. It's always good to get to know someone where you take your car, and ask for him every time you go. I work for Firestone in central NJ. I have Aligned and worked on Members Fiero's in the past.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jay in Atlanta||12-26-2001||02:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierodoug5:<BR><B>All Firestone stores offer lifetime Alignment.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>One of the best investments I've ever made.  I must have gotten four alignments (on two different fieros and my Camaro) so far for the price of about 1 1/2.  At the Firestone I use, there's a large window onto the work floor and I'm able to watch the job they're doing.  I've also asked to be on the floor and inquire about specific things twice and they've let me.<P>Absolutely worth the money.<P>~Jay<BR>Indy 4-Speed<P>||||reg||1
